# What not to upload when deploying from the repository root.
#
# `vercel deploy` runs here, at the repo root, while the Next.js app that
# actually gets built lives in `10_Final_Website/` (the project's Root Directory
# setting). Everything else in this repository is documentation and evidence:
# necessary to the project, irrelevant to the build.
#
# Without this file the CLI uploaded ~129 MB per deploy, of which ~93 MB was
# `docs/_captures/` — 129 PNG frames from visual-regression runs that no build
# step reads. Nothing here changes what is built; it changes how much is sent
# over a domestic uplink before the build can start.
#
# Anything the build needs lives under 10_Final_Website/ and is not listed here.

# Visual-regression frames and browser-session output.
docs/_captures/
.playwright-mcp/
.env-quarantine/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Long-form documentation and archived asset-production material.
Documentation/
brand-os/

# Local build artefacts and dependencies — restated rather than assumed, since
# .vercelignore replaces the default ignore behaviour rather than extending it.
node_modules/
.next/
.git/

# Config backups.
*.rc8-backup
